  legend:'<li><b>ʰ</b>aspiration, a puff of air: tʰ (թ), pʰ (փ), kʰ (ք), tsʰ (ց), chʰ (չ). Without the mark the sound is unaspirated: t (տ), p (պ), k (կ), ts (ծ), ch (ճ)</li><li><b>kh</b>խ, like "ch" in Scottish "loch"</li><li><b>gh</b>ղ, a guttural sound like the French r</li><li><b>ə</b>ը, a short neutral vowel as in "about"</li><li><b>rr</b>ռ, a rolled r; single r (ր) is a light tap</li><li><b>zh</b>ժ, like "s" in "measure"</li><li><b>ye</b>ե at the start of a word; inside a word it is "e". ո at the start is "vo"</li><li><b>´</b>stress falls on the last syllable unless it contains ը</li>',
